  "description": "With its curved blade mimicking a tiger's claw, the karambit was developed as part of the southeast Asian martial discipline of silat. The knife is typically used with a reverse grip, with the finger ring on the index finger. It has been painted using a spider web-patterned hydrographic over a red base coat and finished with a semi-gloss topcoat.\\n\\n<i>Be careful where you walk, you never know where the web is spread</i>",
